      "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
      "body": "## New machine report (2026-08-26)\n\nThis reproduced again on a packaged macOS arm64 install while editing turn `a0f24f12-9b6e-4d4e-bd5e-ee82aac77c2b` in a Codex Chat session.\n\n- Installed AO desktop: `0.12.8-nightly.202608252327`n- Installed Codex CLI: `0.149.1`\n- AO daemon: bundled app daemon, healthy on `127.0.0.1:3001`\n- OS: macOS arm64 (Darwin 27.0.0)\n- Analyzed against current upstream `d32434d9da8868e2a768d0942fade073be06cddc`\n- Observed API result: `POST /api/v1/sessions/{sessionId}/conversation/turns/{turnId}/edit` returned `409 CHAT_RESUME_FAILED`\n\nDurable and provider-side evidence matches this issue exactly:\n\n1. The source Codex thread was `01a0382f-0d9b-7900-b213-884dfcd91815`.\n2. Four edit attempts successfully created four separate Codex rollout files whose `session_meta.forked_from_id` is that source thread.\n3. AO created no durable conversation branch for any fork and kept the original branch active.\n4. A subsequent ordinary user turn completed successfully, confirming the source controller and worktree remained healthy.\n\nThe four abandoned provider forks were:\n\n- `01a03e84-b3cf-70c0-9afe-61857c29ccc6`\n- `01a03e84-c263-77e3-80f7-952d8d189fb5`\n- `01a03e84-c60b-74b3-bf1b-146786b75515`\n- `01a03e84-d5e3-77e1-9123-94fe9e0cadf1`\n\nThis independently confirms the failure is after `thread/fork` succeeds and before AO can activate the replacement branch. It also shows each retry leaves another orphaned Codex fork. PR #4304 appears to address the exact one-writer boundary and is currently green/ready, but still open.",
