    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "body": "## Bug\n\nEditing an earlier human message in a Codex Chat session consistently fails with `CHAT_RESUME_FAILED` instead of creating and activating the edited conversation branch.\n\n**Source:** Reported in AO Chat with an attached screenshot  \n**Analyzed against:** `9c1797cde982c0cdf925c74ea4588cf5f3fbcb57`  \n**AO daemon:** checkout build (`dev`) on `127.0.0.1:3001`  \n**Codex CLI:** `0.148.0`  \n**OS:** macOS arm64  \n**Confidence:** High  \n**Priority:** P1 \u2014 the prompt-edit workflow is broken whenever the edited prompt has a preceding provider turn.\n\n![Reported `CHAT_RESUME_FAILED` error](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Untrivial-ai/agent-orchestrator/issue-assets-codex-edit-active-writer/.issue-assets/codex-edit-active-writer/reported-error.png)\n\n## Reproduction\n\n1. Start a Codex session in Chat mode.\n2. Complete at least two human/assistant turns.\n3. Edit the second human message and submit it.\n4. Observe `the stored provider conversation could not be resumed (CHAT_RESUME_FAILED)`.\n\nA minimized live provider harness reproduces the backend boundary directly:\n\n1. Start a real Codex app-server conversation.\n2. Complete one turn.\n3. Call `thread/fork` through that turn.\n4. While the source app-server remains open, start a second app-server and call `thread/resume` for the fork id.\n\nThis failed three out of three times with app-server error `-32600: thread <id> already has an active writer`. Waiting two seconds did not change the result. Closing the source connection before resume made the same harness pass twice.\n\n## Root Cause\n\n`Service.EditMessage` calls `ChatForker.Fork`, receives the new provider conversation id, and immediately calls `driver.Resume` for that id on a new app-server process. Codex `thread/fork` already loads the new thread and emits `thread/started`, so the source app-server owns the fork as its active writer. The second process cannot resume it.\n\nAO only closes the source controller after the replacement controller has been created and installed. That point is unreachable because replacement resume fails first.\n\nThe existing service fake models `Fork` as returning a passive string and therefore cannot express provider writer ownership. Adapter tests cover fork and resume independently rather than chaining them as the edit flow does.\n\n## Fix\n\nPreserve AO's one-writer and failure-recovery guarantees while changing the edit handoff sequence so a fork is not resumed by a second process while its creating app-server still owns it. Add regression coverage with a writer-aware fake plus an opt-in live Codex fork/resume test.\n\n## Impact\n\n- Editing the first prompt is unaffected because it starts a fresh provider conversation.\n- Editing any later prompt is broken for Codex Chat sessions.\n- The original conversation and worktree remain intact; the edit is refused rather than silently losing history.\n\n## Related\n\n- [PR #3676](https://github.com/Untrivial-ai/agent-orchestrator/pull/3676) \u2014 introduced Codex prompt editing with conversation branches.\n",
